      "backends": ["claude"],
      "url": "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing",
      "read": "2026-09-28",
      "note": "Anthropic first-party API list prices (Model pricing table: base input, 5m cache writes, 1h cache writes, cache hits and refreshes, output). cache_write is the 5-minute cache write (1.25x input) and cache_write_1h the 1-hour one (2x input): a claude turn says which cache it wrote in usage.cache_creation, and one that wrote to the cache without saying is not charged (D-143). Not read, so a turn that used them is under-priced: fast mode and US-only inference (inference_geo, 1.1x). A subscription login is not billed at these prices; its owner sets their own in the price file."
    },
    {
      "backends": ["grok"],
      "url": "https://docs.x.ai/developers/models",
      "read": "2026-09-28",
      "note": "xAI API list prices, the tier for a prompt under 200k tokens; unchanged from table 2026-09-28 (docs.x.ai/docs/models now leads here). xAI bills a request whose prompt reaches 200k tokens at the higher tier for all of its tokens; a CLI turn's usage is summed over several requests, so which tier applied cannot be told from it, and the lower tier can only under-charge. xAI lists no cache-write price and has no 1-hour cache, so cache_write and cache_write_1h are null and a turn that wrote to the cache is not charged."
    }
  ],
